HOW TO INSTALL Rmedio PACKAGE
-----------------------------

1. make sure you have a fairly recent Qt5 library installed:

   On Ubuntu/Linux:
   ---------------
   > sudo aptitude install libqt5-dev
   
   On Mac OSX:
   ----------
   install XCode (see App Store)
   install Qt5 via MacPorts:
   > sudo port install qt5
   > ln -sf /opt/local/libexec/qt5/bin/qmake /usr/local/bin/qmake
   > export SYSTEM_VERSION_COMPAT=0       #necessary as of 2022-10-06 

2. install Rcpp package (version >= 0.11.2) in your R environment:

   R> install.packages("Rcpp")

3. make sure librtdebug is installed or install it:
   
   > git clone https://github.com/jens-maus/librtdebug.git
   > cd librtdebug
   > make distclean
   > make
   > make install
   
4. make sure libmedio is installed or install it:

   > svn co svn+ssh://saturn.fz-rossendorf.de/data/petdev/svn/libmedio/trunk libmedio
   > cd libmedio
   > make distclean
   > make
   > make install

5. cleanup Rmedio:
 
   > (cd Rmedio; ./cleanup)

6. perform 'R CMD INSTALL' or 'rinstall' to install Rmedio:

   > R --no-site-file --no-init-file CMD INSTALL Rmedio
   or:
   > rinstall Rmedio
   
   If you want to override the default install paths of Rcpp you can
   use something like the following example:

   > R --no-site-file --no-init-file CMD INSTALL --configure-args="RCPP_PATH=/Users/vdh/Library/R/cranlib/Rcpp" Rmedio
   
   If you want to override the default install paths of libmedio you can
   use something like the following example:

   > R --no-site-file --no-init-file CMD INSTALL --configure-args="--prefix=/usr/local" Rmedio

7. load Rmedio package in R:

   R> library(Rmedio)
